{
  "opening": "The dateutil library is releasing updates that affect parsing, timezone handling, and recurrence rule generation. The arrow project depends on these behaviors to ensure correct date and time operations. Each change below defines the required observable behavior for the public API.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the relativedelta class must maintain its documented tuple-like interface for representation and iteration without raising errors."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, when parser.parse is called with a tzinfos argument that explicitly returns None for a requested timezone, it must not raise a ValueError but instead handle the missing timezone gracefully."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the functions datetime_ambiguous, datetime_exists, and resolve_imaginary must correctly determine the status of datetimes in ambiguous or non-existent scenarios for various timezone objects like tzfile, tzrange, and tzstr."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the documentation for timezone-related modules must be structured clearly to aid users in understanding timezone usage, though this does not alter runtime behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser function must accept ISO 8601 time strings that use a comma as the decimal separator for fractional seconds, treating them equivalently to those using a period."
    },
    {
      "id": "m37",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser function must interpret the time string T24:00 as midnight on the following day, complying with the ISO 8601 standard."
    },
    {
      "id": "m41",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the tzfile and tzoffset classes must support sub-minute time zone offsets (e.g., 30 minutes and 15 seconds) in Python 3.6 and newer versions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m43",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser.parse_isotime method must correctly handle time strings where the hour component is 24, interpreting them as midnight of the next day."
    },
    {
      "id": "m53",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparse function must accept fractional second components with more than six digits of precision without truncating or raising an error."
    },
    {
      "id": "m58",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the tzfile class must correctly calculate base offset changes during Daylight Saving Time transitions, specifically fixing issues observed with Samoan timezone data."
    },
    {
      "id": "m66",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser and parser functions must recognize the lowercase 'z' character as a valid indicator for UTC timezone in ISO 8601 strings."
    },
    {
      "id": "m68",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the cache_clear and set_cache_size functions must allow management of the LRU cache used by tzoffset, tzstr, and gettz, ensuring transient timezone references do not cause memory leaks while maintaining performance."
    },
    {
      "id": "m80",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the rrule and rruleset classes must parse and respect EXDATE parameters in RRULE strings, excluding specified dates from the generated recurrence set."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure these behaviors are implemented and verified before the next release. This will guarantee compatibility with the arrow project's expectations."
}
